{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarParityZeta4Swap"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.goldenShape_barEven_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.goldenShape_barEven_sq","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L156-L162","doc":"**Golden bar-even `= √5`** (`(barEven ω)² = 5`, REAL): the degenerate branch's\nspecial coordinate is the **real** `√5`, not the cusp's imaginary `√−3`. A real\npole seeds this branch — real coordinate, hence **no CS / no bar-odd `S`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.goldenShape_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.goldenShape_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L151-L154","doc":"**Golden bar-odd `= 1`** (rational): on the degenerate branch the bar-ODD\ncoordinate is rational — the roles are swapped vs the cusp (where bar-EVEN = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.goldenShape_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.goldenShape_inv","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L145-L149","doc":"Golden inverse in shape coordinates: `ω⁻¹ = ω − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.goldenShape_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.goldenShape_sq","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L140-L143","doc":"`ω² = ω + 1` (golden minimal-polynomial rewrite). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.IsGoldenShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.IsGoldenShape","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L137-L138","doc":"The degenerate (golden-ratio) branch: `ω² − ω − 1 = 0`, real root `φ=(1+√5)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_reconstruct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_reconstruct","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L101-L107","doc":"**Reconstruction (Re/Im of `𝔙` from one shape):** the bar-even and bar-odd\ncoordinates reconstruct `2ω`: `barEven ω + barOdd ω = 2ω`.  With\n`barEven ω = 1` and `(barOdd ω)² = −3` this says `2ω = 1 + √−3`, i.e.\n`ω = (1 + √−3)/2 = e^{iπ/3}` — the complete cusp shape recovered from its\n`Vol`(=1) and `CS`(=√−3) coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_sixth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_sixth","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L96-L99","doc":"`ω⁶ = 1`: primitive sixth root of unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_cube","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L89-L94","doc":"`ω³ = −1`: the cusp shape is a primitive sixth root of unity (`ω = e^{iπ/3}`),\nso `ω³ = e^{iπ} = −1`.  The root-of-unity structure the bar-odd phase channel\naccumulates in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_barOdd_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_barOdd_sq","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L80-L87","doc":"**The cusp modulus `√−3`:** the bar-odd coordinate squares to `−3`, i.e.\n`(barOdd ω)² = −3`.  This is the figure-eight trace-field discriminant / the\nNeumann–Zagier cusp modulus `τ ∝ √−3` — proved exactly, generic field.\nArchimedean: `barOdd ω = 2i·sin(π/3) = √−3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L76-L78","doc":"**Bar-odd coordinate `= 2ω − 1`** (`Im 𝔙 = CS` side): `barOdd ω = ω − ω⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L71-L74","doc":"**Bar-even coordinate `= 1`** (`Re 𝔙 = Vol` side): `barEven ω = ω + ω⁻¹ = 1`,\nthe amphichiral / anchor-stable part.  Archimedean: `2cos(π/3) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_inv","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L63-L69","doc":"**The inverse in shape coordinates:** `ω⁻¹ = 1 − ω`.  The bar involution\n`ω ↦ ω⁻¹` acts as the reflection `ω ↦ 1 − ω` on the cusp shape (the\n`z ↦ 1 − 1/z ↦ …` tetrahedral symmetry, here at the symmetric point). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_sq","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L58-L61","doc":"`ω² = ω − 1` (the minimal-polynomial rewrite). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.cuspShape_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L52-L56","doc":"The cusp shape is nonzero (`Φ₆(0) = 1 ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.IsCuspShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity.IsCuspShape","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L47-L50","doc":"The figure-eight cusp shape `ω` is a root of the cyclotomic `Φ₆(z) = z²−z+1`\n(trace field `ℚ(√−3)`).  We take that minimal polynomial as the defining\nhypothesis; the archimedean realisation is `ω = e^{iπ/3}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}